sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant CLI as CLI (corvus/cli.py)
    participant Reg as Tool Registry
    participant MCP as MCP Client (MCPManager)
    participant FS as Filesystem server
    participant TAV as Tavily server
    participant RAG as docs-rag server
    participant Agent as Agentic Loop
    participant LLM as LLM (Groq)

    User->>CLI: python -m corvus --workspace D:\corvus-demo
    CLI->>MCP: connect_all(servers.json, workspace)
    MCP->>MCP: load servers.json, expand ${WORKSPACE} ${PYTHON} ${TAVILY_API_KEY}
    MCP->>FS: start "npx server-filesystem D:\corvus-demo" (stdio)
    FS-->>MCP: initialize OK
    MCP->>FS: tools/list
    FS-->>MCP: 14 tools (read_text_file, write_file, edit_file, ...)
    MCP->>TAV: connect over HTTPS (API key in URL)
    TAV-->>MCP: 5 tools (tavily_search, tavily_extract, ...)
    MCP->>RAG: start "python -m rag_server.server" (stdio)
    RAG-->>MCP: initialize OK
    Note over RAG: background thread loads ChromaDB,<br/>embedding model and cross-encoder
    MCP->>RAG: tools/list
    RAG-->>MCP: search_docs(query, k)
    MCP-->>Reg: 20 MCP tools, named server__tool
    Reg-->>CLI: + run_command, grep_code (local)
    CLI->>Agent: Agent(registry, model)
    Agent->>Agent: hide 9 duplicate/rare tools, shrink schemas
    Agent->>LLM: bind_tools(13 tool schemas)
    CLI-->>User: banner, model, mode, "filesystem (8), local (2), tavily (2), docs-rag (1)"
    User->>CLI: /tools
    CLI-->>User: table of tools per server, which ones ask first
